  "experiment": {
    "notes": "Nine predeclared pooled candidates; one finalist per floor and heads group freezes from development only. The scale floor is symmetric softplus plus min_scale. Equivalence labels assert neural fit-state equality only, not whole-curve equality. After group selection and before evaluation, an external recorded protocol compares the two group winners with the raw incumbent. A candidate is eligible only when its equal-cell development CRPS is strictly below the incumbent and, for every index on paired rows, abs(count(PIT < 0.05)/N - 0.05) is no greater than the incumbent (tolerance 1e-12). Choose the eligible candidate with lowest development relative CRPS; ties prefer incumbent then lexical name; otherwise retain incumbent. This external primary freeze is not a machine guard. The existing CLI still evaluates both winners plus all three controls. Empirical and incumbent controls disable calibration; pooled MLP and candidates enable it.",
